  {
   "id": "kospi-chip-rally",
   "group": "Korea",
   "headline": "KOSPI extends its rebound as chip stocks surge",
   "when": "Wed 11 Nov · Seoul close",
   "what": "KOSPI rose 136.23 points, or 2.6%, to 5,375.36 on Wednesday. It was the second straight gain after a 4.39% rise on Tuesday. SK hynix gained 5.36% and Samsung Electronics 3.57%. Foreigners bought a net 655.26 billion won of shares. The won firmed to 1,333.6 per dollar from 1,337.5.",
   "why": "Korea is 16.3% of the portfolio, mostly through SCBKEQTG, whose largest holdings are the chipmakers that led the move. This morning the dashboard prices SCBKEQTG at its 9 Nov NAV, so KOSPI's roughly 4.4% rise since then is not yet in the number. Newer fund NAVs usually arrive at the 11:30 refresh.",
