   "id": "us-cpi-ai-rebound",
   "group": "United States",
   "headline": "Hot inflation raises Fed hike bets, but AI shares still lead a rally",
   "when": "Wed 11 Nov · US session",
   "what": "US October consumer prices rose faster than forecast: 0.3% in one report, 0.4% in another. Traders put about an 86% chance on a quarter-point Fed hike on 9 Dec, per CoinDesk. Stocks still rose: the S&P 500 closed up 1.31% and the Nasdaq 1.60%. CoreWeave jumped after raising its revenue forecast, and chip names such as Nvidia and Micron gained. Bond markets were closed for Veterans Day.",
   "why": "About 25% of the portfolio sits in US stocks, mostly through the S&P 500 funds. Higher rates are a risk for richly valued shares, while the AI rebound is what is lifting the index. The next test is the 9 Dec Fed decision.",
